    "annotations": [
      {
        "id": "a001",
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "**Torque-speed curve.** A dynamometer (MSf) turns the horn from -8 to 20 rad/s while the goal is far ahead, so the firmware asks for full PWM. Servo/tau_l is the torque at the horn: the current-limited stall line (i_limit) then the back-EMF line to the free speed v_bat/kt, minus the friction and the armature torque.",
        "x": 0,
        "y": -200,
        "w": 700,
        "h": 120,
        "color": "blue"
      },
      {
        "id": "a002",
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "XL330Rigid has no armature of its own (the joint carries it), so Servo/Transmit/y here is kt i minus the friction, without the armature torque of the ramp. The encoder input is held at 0: the goal is 1000 rad ahead either way.",
        "x": 0,
        "y": -320,
        "w": 700,
        "h": 100,
        "color": "blue"
      }
    ]
  },
